From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:53:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 87/99] v8: e2k: put literals of up to 32 bits in the command

LoongArch has 12-bit immediates, and the selector and the macro assembler
loaded a wider constant into a scratch register first. An e2k command
carries 32- and 64-bit literals: add, sub, and, or, xor and the bit test
take a literal of up to 32 bits from the selector (sign-extended, as the
Word32 values are), and the macro assembler puts any non-relocatable
literal in the operation (addli_d, andli, orli, xorli in the layer).
---
 chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/assembler-e2k.cc   |  4 ++++
 chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/assembler-e2k.h    |  5 +++++
 chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/la_asm.h           |  6 ++++++
 .../v8/src/codegen/e2k/macro-assembler-e2k.cc  | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 .../backend/e2k/instruction-selector-e2k.cc    |  8 +++++++-
 5 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

